<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/14th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Auray</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1364">1364</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-breton-succession">War of the Breton Succession</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Auray, fought on 29 September 1364 in southern Brittany, was the decisive battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-breton-succession">War of the Breton Succession</a>. An Anglo-Breton army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/john-of-montfort">John of Montfort</a> and Sir John Chandos defeated the Franco-Breton forces of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-of-blois">Charles of Blois</a>, who was killed, while <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bertrand-du-guesclin">Bertrand du Guesclin</a> was captured. The Treaty of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerande">Guérande</a> in 1365 recognised Montfort as Duke John IV.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-auray.jpg" alt="Battle of Auray" width="320" height="283" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Loyset Liédet · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Battle_of_Auray_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
